00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:29.000
Whitney Hodges: and co-owners of Wedding Industry Ads.

00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:33.000
Myla Li Photos: Perfect. Nice to finally meet you, Whitney.

00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:35.000
Whitney Hodges: So nice to meet you. How's your day going?

00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:43.000
Myla Li Photos: Not too bad. I'm currently at work, so I have a conference room, so I can't turn my camera on, but yeah.

00:00:43.000 --> 00:00:53.000
Whitney Hodges: Okay, no worries, I totally understand. Um, so I know you said that you shoot most of your weddings in California, but you're not based there, is that right? Where are you?

00:00:51.000 --> 00:00:54.000
Myla Li Photos: Yes, I'm in Seattle.

00:00:54.000 --> 00:00:56.000
Whitney Hodges: Okay, awesome. All right.

00:00:54.000 --> 00:00:59.000
Myla Li Photos: The goal is to eventually move to California, but yeah.

00:00:59.000 --> 00:01:16.000
Whitney Hodges: Love that. Yeah, so, um, yeah, I'm excited to hear more about your business, uh, kind of where you are right now, what your, your goals are for it in terms of, um, yeah, getting you, getting you to California, doing things full-time, um, and am just happy to chat with you about the.

00:01:16.000 --> 00:01:22.000
Whitney Hodges: Meta Ads Accelerator and answer any questions that you might have to see if we think it's a good fit.

00:01:21.000 --> 00:01:38.000
Myla Li Photos: Perfect. Yeah. I'm trying to think about, I guess, just background. I've been doing this for about four years now, so still kind of early on, even though it feels like it's been so long. I started doing them up in the Pacific Northwest in Portland, actually.

00:01:29.000 --> 00:01:30.000
Whitney Hodges: Mm-hmm.

00:01:32.000 --> 00:01:33.000
Whitney Hodges: Yeah.

00:01:38.000 --> 00:01:39.000
Whitney Hodges: Mm-hmm.

00:01:38.000 --> 00:01:46.000
Myla Li Photos: Uh, and then I moved to Seattle for my job. I don't love Seattle, I just don't like the market up here. Um…

00:01:44.000 --> 00:01:46.000
Whitney Hodges: Yeah. Mm-hmm.

00:01:46.000 --> 00:01:52.000
Myla Li Photos: either my ideal clients just really aren't here, honestly, and I hate the weather, so, um…

00:01:50.000 --> 00:01:52.000
Whitney Hodges: Hahaha.

00:01:52.000 --> 00:02:04.000
Myla Li Photos: I've just been loving… I just started, like, marketing towards LA a couple years ago, and I've just, like, gotten the majority of my inquiries and everything from there, and planner relationships through Instagram, which has been great. I think…

00:01:57.000 --> 00:01:59.000
Whitney Hodges: Mm-hmm.

00:02:03.000 --> 00:02:05.000
Whitney Hodges: Yep.

00:02:04.000 --> 00:02:19.000
Myla Li Photos: I think right now, where I'm at, is just, like, wanting more visibility, and just trying to figure out, like, without, um, constantly, just because of having, like, another job, without, like, constantly engaging with people on Instagram, being able to, like, get my name out there more often.

00:02:16.000 --> 00:02:17.000
Whitney Hodges: Sure.

00:02:20.000 --> 00:02:35.000
Whitney Hodges: Yeah, yeah, no, that totally makes sense. Yeah, the churn of kind of always being on social media can definitely take a toll and it can be frustrating for sure when it's like, I don't know, you put out a post or a reel or something and you…

00:02:35.000 --> 00:02:54.000
Whitney Hodges: you know, think that it's gonna get great engagement or great visibility, and then it doesn't, or you put something out and you just see that it, like, fizzles really quickly. Um, and that's one of the reasons that we created the Meta Ads Accelerator, to really be able to show wedding pros how you can take some of your best pieces of content.

00:02:54.000 --> 00:03:03.000
Whitney Hodges: And turn it into, you know, ads that are always reaching new couples, new people, um, every day to get more visibility on the business.

00:03:03.000 --> 00:03:16.000
Myla Li Photos: Yeah, totally. Especially, too, because, like, I feel like a lot of, like, California weddings, they're couples that aren't actually in California. It's, like, destinations, so trying to figure out ways to, like, target those couples. Um, in my mind, that strategy seems a way to go.

00:03:09.000 --> 00:03:11.000
Whitney Hodges: Right. Mm-hmm.

00:03:16.000 --> 00:03:34.000
Whitney Hodges: Yeah, totally. So, um, yeah, so it sounds like, you know, referrals and the Instagram marketing have kind of been working for you so far, um, but I also heard you say that you feel like, you know, sometimes when people see your pricing, or maybe when you have a consultation, then you don't end up.

00:03:34.000 --> 00:03:40.000
Whitney Hodges: hearing from them afterwards? Was… was that accurate? Is that kind of what you're seeing on your end?

00:03:37.000 --> 00:03:39.000
Myla Li Photos: Yes.

00:03:39.000 --> 00:03:43.000
Myla Li Photos: Yes. That is usually where I, like, lose people.

00:03:43.000 --> 00:03:47.000
Whitney Hodges: Mm-hmm. What do you think the disconnect might be there?

00:03:48.000 --> 00:04:04.000
Myla Li Photos: I can't tell. I don't know if it is, like, pricing, if it's, like, the pricing is, like, too high or is it too low in a way, like, for people, or if it's just, like, style. I feel like it's a… I'm talking to people about this and just theorizing, I don't actually know.

00:03:54.000 --> 00:03:56.000
Whitney Hodges: Mm-hmm.

00:04:03.000 --> 00:04:04.000
Whitney Hodges: Mm-hmm.

00:04:04.000 --> 00:04:07.000
Myla Li Photos: At, like, this price point, it just feels like…

00:04:07.000 --> 00:04:16.000
Myla Li Photos: there's just so many, like, the talent for this, like, price point is, like, very similar. I feel like it's really difficult to… to really suss out what it is, but…

00:04:11.000 --> 00:04:12.000
Whitney Hodges: Mm-hmm.

00:04:15.000 --> 00:04:21.000
Whitney Hodges: Got it. Yeah, so there's kind of a lot of competition at your price point, is that kind of what I'm hearing?

00:04:19.000 --> 00:04:23.000
Myla Li Photos: Yeah, in my market, yeah, for sure.

00:04:21.000 --> 00:04:36.000
Whitney Hodges: Okay, yeah, yeah, no, that totally makes sense. Um, and so, yeah, that can oftentimes be where it's just kind of a numbers game, right? Like, you need a higher volume of leads to come in to really be, you know, closing the volume.

00:04:31.000 --> 00:04:33.000
Myla Li Photos: Exactly.

00:04:36.000 --> 00:04:43.000
Whitney Hodges: Um, that you'd like. Um, so at this point, how many weddings are you doing a year?

00:04:43.000 --> 00:04:51.000
Myla Li Photos: It really varies. This year was super, super low, unfortunately. I had 4 weddings this year, but the previous years I've had about, like, 12 to 15.

00:04:46.000 --> 00:04:48.000
Whitney Hodges: Okay.

00:04:51.000 --> 00:04:59.000
Whitney Hodges: Okay, got it. Um, so is the goal for 2027 to kind of get back to that 12 to 15 mark?

00:04:58.000 --> 00:05:09.000
Myla Li Photos: Yes, yeah, like, again, just, like, trying to increase, like you said, like, numbers game. Just, like, the more eyes, the more, like, inquiries, and try to figure… go that way.

00:05:03.000 --> 00:05:05.000
Whitney Hodges: Mm-hmm.

00:05:08.000 --> 00:05:24.000
Whitney Hodges: Mm-hmm. Mm-hmm. Okay. Got it. So, in kind of this past year being kind of a weird year, I mean, are you kind of feeling like, you know, what you had been doing in your marketing is no longer kind of working the way that it…

00:05:24.000 --> 00:05:29.000
Whitney Hodges: used to, or has there been some other sort of change there, you think?

00:05:28.000 --> 00:05:51.000
Myla Li Photos: Oh, yeah, good question. I probably should have. So at the beginning of this year, I was planning to move to Arizona because my boyfriend got a job there, and then it just fell through. Like, life stuff happened. That's totally fine. But all of my marketing, like, for about a good, like, five months into the year, I was pretty much, like, targeting Arizona. So I switched all my SEO. Yeah, so I feel like that was, like, the biggest thing. I switched all my SEO. I was.

00:05:36.000 --> 00:05:38.000
Whitney Hodges: Oh, okay.

00:05:47.000 --> 00:05:48.000
Whitney Hodges: Got it.

00:05:48.000 --> 00:05:50.000
Whitney Hodges: Mm-hmm.

00:05:51.000 --> 00:06:09.000
Myla Li Photos: like, outreach to all these planners and everything, and then, like, I posted on Instagram and, like, announced it to everyone, and so everyone probably thinks I'm just in Arizona. Um, so I feel like that, like, messed up a lot of… just, like, in, you know, just, like, referrals and stuff, and everyone's like, oh, she's there, but I didn't really…

00:06:00.000 --> 00:06:02.000
Whitney Hodges: Mm-hmm.

00:06:09.000 --> 00:06:24.000
Myla Li Photos: I don't wanna like take it back. So I felt weird about that. So I've been trying to like do in-person stuff so people still know that I'm here, at least in Seattle and like, and then all my SEO and like everything else, Instagram's still been targeting LA and California and stuff.

00:06:11.000 --> 00:06:13.000
Whitney Hodges: Yeah. Mm-hmm.

00:06:17.000 --> 00:06:19.000
Whitney Hodges: Mm-hmm.

00:06:24.000 --> 00:06:27.000
Whitney Hodges: Got it. Okay, yeah, I could definitely…

00:06:25.000 --> 00:06:28.000
Myla Li Photos: But I think that's like what happened.

00:06:27.000 --> 00:06:47.000
Whitney Hodges: Yeah, I could definitely see how like the potential location change may have kind of shifted some things in terms of your your visibility for the the La market for sure. I think I saw you mentioned something about, you know, kind of the the SEO efforts for California or La but that.

00:06:36.000 --> 00:06:38.000
Myla Li Photos: Mm-hmm.

00:06:47.000 --> 00:06:56.000
Whitney Hodges: that maybe you're kind of just seeing some shortcomings there, or feeling like ads are a better fit, or somebody maybe recommended ads being a better fit than going the route of SEO, is that right?

00:06:56.000 --> 00:07:04.000
Myla Li Photos: Yes, yeah, I'm trying to do both. So I do have, like, I just actually, like, 30 minutes ago, I was on a call with someone to, like.

00:07:04.000 --> 00:07:17.000
Myla Li Photos: do at least, like, the foundational portions of my SEO, and, like, get some landing pages and blogs out, so… I have someone working on that, and then… but the majority of, I guess, like, advice from my business coach was just…

00:07:06.000 --> 00:07:08.000
Whitney Hodges: Mm-hmm.

00:07:17.000 --> 00:07:26.000
Myla Li Photos: Just visibility, essentially, too, of making sure that, like, my face, my brand, my name is out there, and thinks that ads would probably be better.

00:07:18.000 --> 00:07:20.000
Whitney Hodges: Okay.

00:07:26.000 --> 00:07:45.000
Whitney Hodges: Mm-hmm. Yeah, no, no, that, that totally, um, makes sense. And, um, Meta ads in particular, we just see them being, like, so great for photographers because of the, the creative elements of them, right? Like, the fact that you're really getting a, being able to showcase your work, to showcase more about who you are.

00:07:45.000 --> 00:07:50.000
Whitney Hodges: your personality a bit in a way, right?

00:07:50.000 --> 00:08:07.000
Whitney Hodges: So what we typically recommend there, like what the, the strategies that we're teaching inside the Meta Ads Accelerator is we call it a full funnel approach. Um, because have you, have you dabbled in Meta Ads for your business at all before? Or are you, how familiar are you? Okay.

00:08:05.000 --> 00:08:16.000
Myla Li Photos: No. One of my friends shared this course with me that she had, and I just couldn't do it. I was like, I don't understand what's going on.

00:08:13.000 --> 00:08:15.000
Whitney Hodges: Yes.

00:08:15.000 --> 00:08:22.000
Whitney Hodges: Yeah, yeah. No, it can be super overwhelming, and definitely inside the Meta Ads Excel… Meta Ads, um…

00:08:22.000 --> 00:08:39.000
Whitney Hodges: platform, right? Just, like, in your campaigns, in your account, it can feel… it definitely just can feel overwhelming in terms of setting things up, because it's, like, there are so many different options in terms of different campaign objectives and different settings to turn on or turn off, and…

00:08:24.000 --> 00:08:25.000
Myla Li Photos: Mm-hmm.

00:08:39.000 --> 00:08:58.000
Whitney Hodges: creating custom audiences, um, you know, installing the pixel and getting tracking right, you know, things like that, um, that it's like… it's also, like, if you, um, make a wrong move there, it really can have a negative impact, um, as well. So, another reason that we've created the Meta Ads Accelerator.

00:08:53.000 --> 00:08:55.000
Myla Li Photos: Mm-hmm.

00:08:58.000 --> 00:09:17.000
Whitney Hodges: I'd really like to do, you know, the majority of the heavy lifting when it comes to helping you get your ad account set up, getting tracking, you know, in place on your website or landing pages, creating those custom audiences for you, and actually going into your ad account and having our team to be the ones that are.

00:09:17.000 --> 00:09:34.000
Whitney Hodges: Um, building the campaigns, launching the campaigns for you. Because what we find is that, um, it's so much easier, you know, as a wedding pro or, you know, a business owner in general, right? If you have a foundation, if you have a framework.

00:09:34.000 --> 00:09:52.000
Whitney Hodges: Of like, these are the best practices, this is the way to set it up, right? You already have a campaign that's set up for you. If in the future, you then want to duplicate that campaign, or make tweaks to it, or launch a new ad, or something like that on your own, it's so much easier to go about it that way than it is to just have to be like.

00:09:52.000 --> 00:10:02.000
Whitney Hodges: starting from scratch and following, you know, along, you know, an over-the-shoulder training from a course or a YouTube video or something like that. Does that make sense?

00:10:02.000 --> 00:10:11.000
Myla Li Photos: Oh, totally. That's exactly what I'm looking for. Yeah, just someone to set it up and get it looking better and figuring it out. It's so difficult.

00:10:10.000 --> 00:10:30.000
Whitney Hodges: Okay, perfect, yeah. So, you know, part of it's gonna be us kind of doing that work inside of your ad account, but also educating you on what we're doing, right? Kind of, like, showing you the ropes, so that if you go into your ad account and are looking at things, you're not, like, completely in the dark of, like, what is this? What… what does this all mean?

00:10:18.000 --> 00:10:20.000
Myla Li Photos: Mm-hmm.

00:10:21.000 --> 00:10:23.000
Myla Li Photos: Perfect.

00:10:30.000 --> 00:10:47.000
Whitney Hodges: Right? The part where it is very collaborative, I would say, and is going to require, you know, some time and attention on your end is going to come to, like, more of, like, the creative assets aspect of it, right?

00:10:45.000 --> 00:10:46.000
Myla Li Photos: Mm-hmm.

00:10:47.000 --> 00:11:02.000
Whitney Hodges: Um, first and foremost, what we recommend for any ad strategy, whether running ads on Meta or you're running ads on Google, is to send those ads to a dedicated landing page, specifically for ads traffic. So…

00:10:53.000 --> 00:10:54.000
Myla Li Photos: All right.

00:11:01.000 --> 00:11:03.000
Myla Li Photos: Mm, mm-hmm.

00:11:02.000 --> 00:11:24.000
Whitney Hodges: a little bit different right than just like sending them to your full blown website. And the reason that we recommend that is because we see that conversions are are better when you go that route right? It's a long form landing page where they have one clear next step, one action to take which would be to inquire with you.

00:11:24.000 --> 00:11:39.000
Whitney Hodges: Versus when, you know, they go to your website and there are, you know, so many different options. They can check out galleries, they can check out blog posts, they could go over to social media pages, which is all great when people are in the research phase.

00:11:39.000 --> 00:11:45.000
Whitney Hodges: Um, but when you're paying people to, you know, for that visibility and to go to a specific, um.

00:11:45.000 --> 00:11:56.000
Whitney Hodges: URL, right? We really want to try to capture their attention as best we can, and get them to convert into an inquiry. Um, so that's kind of what the thinking there is.

00:11:56.000 --> 00:12:12.000
Whitney Hodges: Um, so inside the Ads Accelerator, there's gonna be, um, a good amount of, you know, resources for you, kind of frameworks in terms of what are the elements and components of making, you know, just a really strong.

00:12:12.000 --> 00:12:31.000
Whitney Hodges: landing page for your ads traffic. And then, from there, you can submit the landing page to us for our personalized feedback, like, we can let you know if there are any tweaks that we would recommend making, or any opportunities that we're seeing before we start pushing ads traffic.

00:12:23.000 --> 00:12:24.000
Myla Li Photos: Mm-hmm, okay.

00:12:31.000 --> 00:12:42.000
Whitney Hodges: to that page. Um, so I'm curious, kind of, how that sounds on your end, like, if you think creating a landing page like that would be something that you would have the bandwidth for at this point.

00:12:42.000 --> 00:12:54.000
Myla Li Photos: Oh, totally, yeah. And I liked that you… you already answered, like, one of my questions of just being like, oh, like, are you guys gonna, like, help with, like, how I should do that? Like, what works, um, well from, like, what you guys have seen? Okay, so that's perfect, yeah.

00:12:43.000 --> 00:12:44.000
Whitney Hodges: Okay.

00:12:54.000 --> 00:13:14.000
Whitney Hodges: Yeah, so it's, like, just a lot of really great examples, right, of landing pages from, like, current and past clients, where you can just kind of see, okay, yeah, here's where we recommend having, you know, a testimonial to start, and then, like, these are the great components of your hero section, and, like, these are the other things that we want you to hit on on this page to really help your ideal clients.

00:13:14.000 --> 00:13:29.000
Whitney Hodges: Um, self-qualify, um, or, or self-disqualify for that matter, right? Because, you know, we want the inquiries that are coming in to feel, um, aligned for you, not just be, you know, price shoppers or people that are gonna ghost after they see the price.

00:13:29.000 --> 00:13:31.000
Whitney Hodges: Um, or things along those lines, you know?

00:13:31.000 --> 00:13:32.000
Myla Li Photos: Mm-hmm.

00:13:32.000 --> 00:13:38.000
Whitney Hodges: Okay, cool. So, um, beyond that, the, um, you know, the other thing…

00:13:38.000 --> 00:14:02.000
Whitney Hodges: that would be in your court would be as far as like the ad creatives and the ad copy. So again, lots of resources inside. You know lots of examples and kind of frameworks. But ultimately, you know, you would be deciding. Okay, you know, these are the reels that I want to turn into an ad, or these are, you know, the photos that I, you know, would want to feature as an ad creative or.

00:14:02.000 --> 00:14:18.000
Whitney Hodges: you know, kind of used together as a carousel sort of thing. And again, you can, you know, submit what you have in mind to us for our feedback. And we're, you know, happy to share more there, right? And kind of let you know if we feel like.

00:14:18.000 --> 00:14:33.000
Whitney Hodges: Anything could be improved upon, or if messaging or positioning could be tightened, things like that. But when you're ready for those ads to go live, there's just a really simple submission form that you fill out, and then those go to us. And then Jacqueline gets the ads.

00:14:33.000 --> 00:14:37.000
Whitney Hodges: up and running typically within the next like 48 hours.

00:14:36.000 --> 00:14:38.000
Myla Li Photos: Oh, awesome.

00:14:38.000 --> 00:14:53.000
Whitney Hodges: Yeah, yeah. And so then, once your ads are, uh, running, you, um, can call in to, you know, Jacqueline's office hours weekly, uh, if that, you know, works with your, your schedule, and, um, she can.

00:14:53.000 --> 00:15:09.000
Whitney Hodges: you know, pull up her screen, or you can screen share. You guys can look inside of your ad account together to kind of assess the data. See if any you know, tweaks or kind of changes would be recommended really kind of help. You understand what's actually going on inside.

00:15:08.000 --> 00:15:10.000
Myla Li Photos: Mm-hmm.

00:15:09.000 --> 00:15:28.000
Whitney Hodges: the ad account, um, but then there are also resources, too, to just kind of help you understand ad performance, right? Like, what all the metrics mean, um, and really kind of digging into your funnel as a whole, right? Like, you know, if you're seeing, um, a great click-through rate, but people are getting to the landing page, and you're not seeing.

00:15:28.000 --> 00:15:47.000
Whitney Hodges: as many conversions there as you'd like, well then, that's when it's kind of time to revisit the landing page and maybe make some edits there. Or, you know, if people are inquiring, but then, you know, you're kind of not hearing anything from them after, you know, initial email or text touchpoints or things like that, again, like, maybe kind of time…

00:15:47.000 --> 00:16:08.000
Whitney Hodges: time to tweak what that initial communication is. So you know, there's definitely a heavy emphasis on ads and getting your ads set up the right way. But ads don't work in isolation, right? It is very like holistic. And what happens after someone comes in from an ad. That's the really important part as well. So we're here to support you with that, too.

00:16:08.000 --> 00:16:15.000
Myla Li Photos: No, that's super awesome. That's great to hear. That's not just like, here you go and then bye.

